# Xcode, CocoaPods and Firebase rules lived here from a template this project
# never used — it is Node scripts, plain HTML and a Cloudflare Worker, and
# nothing matching them has ever been tracked. Removed rather than left to
# suggest a shape the repository does not have.

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?
# Licensed question-bank content — never commit these.
# Your ACCSAP export and anything derived from it stays on your own devices.
content/
*ACCSAP*.html
*.accsap.json

# Stage 1 build output — contains a copy of the licensed content.
dist/

# Local build output — contains a copy of the licensed content.
build/
source/

# Python bytecode from tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Transcript of the last failing verify run — quotes licensed suite output.
tests/last-run.log

# Knowledge graphs written by `graphify` — graph.json, GRAPH_REPORT.md,
# graph.html. Its walker respects .gitignore by default, so a default run skips
# content/, build/, dist/ and source/ — every one of them ignored above. But
# `--no-gitignore` is one flag, and a .graphifyignore can re-include a path on
# its own; either way the graph then carries excerpts of the licensed question
# text under a name that suggests nothing of the kind. leak-guard refuses this
# prefix too: a .gitignore entry is a default, and only the guard is a boundary.
graphify-out/

# Local artifacts from running the suite by hand. None of these belongs in the
# repository and two of them are builds, so they carry the licensed corpus —
# leak-guard rule 3 refuses anything over 1 MB, but only once `npm run hooks`
# has been run on that clone, and a laptop that has never run it is exactly
# where these accumulate.
*.zip
*.log
figdiag.js
verify-fails.log

# Installed packages — ts-fsrs is a dev-time oracle for verify-oracle,
# regenerated by hand with tools/gen-fsrs-oracle.js. Nothing here ships.
node_modules/

# Two more things graphify writes, found by reading the installed package
# rather than guessing from it. (An earlier version of this block did guess:
# it listed `.graphify-bak/` as a directory and `.graphify_*.json` at the root.
# Neither is where they live — the second sits inside graphify-out/, already
# ignored above — and its comment claimed `graphify update .` writes to the
# repository root, which it does not. graphify-out/ is where it writes.)
#
# A repo-local custom LLM provider config, `.graphify/providers.json`
# (graphify/llm.py, `_custom_providers_path(global_=False)`). graphify's own
# comment on it: a custom provider "receives the full corpus plus the user's
# API key". A file that says where the corpus and the key are sent is not one
# to commit.
.graphify/
# The backup `graphify install` takes of a settings file before rewriting it:
# `.claude/settings.json.graphify-bak` (graphify/install.py). A suffix on a
# file, not a directory — so the pattern is a suffix too.
*.graphify-bak

# Memorizer (memorizer/) — build output, and a place to keep PDFs you test it
# with. The app reads a PDF in the browser and never stores it; nothing a user
# studies belongs in the repository, whosever it is.
dist-memorizer/
memorizer/samples/
